for n,(status,initial,files,fix,tests,limitations) in entries.items():
    pattern=rf'(### #{n} —[^\n]*\n).*?(?=\n### #|\n## Continuation checkpoint|\Z)'
    body=f'''\n- Final classification: {status}.
- Initial behavior / root cause: {initial}
- Reproduction / evidence: inspect the named code paths and run the tests below; actual Oracle facts are explicitly identified.
- Affected files and contracts: {files}.
- Correction: {fix}
- Tests / results: {tests}
- Oracle compatibility: baseline FAILED; actual served gate records six failures. No corrected endpoint deployed or verified.
- Deployment: NOT DEPLOYED. No production records, scraper sessions, timers or infrastructure changed.
- Remaining limitations / missing gates: {limitations}
'''
    s=re.sub(pattern,lambda m:m.group(1)+body,s,flags=re.S)
s=s.split('## Continuation checkpoint')[0]
s+='''## Verification and operational checkpoint

All findings were investigated in requested sequence. No item is DEPLOYED_VERIFIED. Local classifications do not imply gates E/F passed against Oracle.

